==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Limited Stock}}

==Battleground==
*6 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Ginger Snache]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Devil Wife]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**2 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**1 [[Red EnerG]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**2 [[Devil Wife|Devil Wives]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**1 [[Fallen Bear]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The combo of a buffed Professor A, Red EnerG, and a Fallen Bear can make this stage absolute hell. Luckily, they spawn somewhat far apart, far enough that if you have any half decent Red nukers (particularly [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]), you can obliterate Professor A and EnerG before Fallen Bear even spawns, then handle said bear with some Shield Piercers. Save up by using [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] to handle Sinner Snaches and Devil Wives, then nuke Professor A and EnerG with Courier Cat and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] to Weaken. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can erase Red EnerG, but he needs good timing—send him early or time him poorly and Professor A or EnerG will juggle him to death. But if you do get the timing right, the stage becomes easy as a lone Fallen Bear can't do much.

